==Old Norse==
{{number box|non}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*fedwōr}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*kʷetwṓr}}, the neuter form of {{der|non|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}. The elder form with ''-ð-'' is still visible in the name of {{m|non|Fjaðryndaland|'''Fjaðr'''yndaland}} ({{cog|gmq-osw|Fiæþrundaland|'''Fiæþr'''undaland}}). Proto-Germanic intervocalic d wad pronounced ''ð.''

